<section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Knowledge Base</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">
            Common questions regarding Verdis technology, VRDX coin mechanics, and eco architecture.
        </p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="faq-accordion-wrap reveal">
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">What is the native coin ticker for Verdis? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                The native coin ticker is <strong>VRDX</strong>. Never confuse this with older or placeholder tickers. The total maximum coin supply is fixed at <strong>100,000,000,000 VRDX</strong> (100 Billion VRDX).
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">How does Verdis achieve verifiable carbon-negative operation? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                Verdis operates under Green Delegated Proof of Stake (DPoS), consuming a fraction of a percent of legacy PoW energy. Additionally, on-chain runtime pallets automatically direct protocol fees toward verified carbon credit retirements and timber reforestation logging.
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">What framework powers the Verdis blockchain? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                Verdis is built in Rust using the Substrate framework (Polkadot SDK). This grants the protocol type safety, high execution speed, WASM smart contract support via <code>pallet-contracts</code>, and forkless runtime upgrade capability.
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">What are the vesting terms for presale participants? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                Seed and Private presale allocations feature a <strong>60-day linear vesting schedule</strong> starting at TGE. Public and final presale allocations feature a <strong>30-day linear vesting schedule</strong>.
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">How do I connect to the RPC endpoint or Explorer? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                The public JSON-RPC endpoint is hosted at <code>https://rpc.verdischain.com</code> over HTTPS and WebSockets. You can inspect blocks and extrinsics live at <code>explorer.verdischain.com</code>.
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-card" onclick="toggleFaqCard(this)">
            <div class="faq-accordion-head">How can developers deploy smart contracts on Verdis? <span class="faq-toggle-icon">+</span></div>
            <div class="faq-accordion-body">
                Developers can write smart contracts in ink! or Rust, compile them to WebAssembly (.wasm bytecode), and deploy them via <code>pallet-contracts</code> using the Verdis Developer Portal or cargo-contract tooling.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

