<section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="card-glass reveal">
        <h3 style="font-size:24px; color:var(--accent); margin-bottom:16px;">Comprehensive Technical Protocol Specification</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:16px;">
            The Verdis blockchain platform represents a significant leap forward in green distributed ledger technology. By leveraging the Substrate framework and Rust language, Verdis provides formal type safety, memory guarantees, and high execution speed without sacrificing decentralization.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:16px;">
            At the heart of Verdis lies a modular pallet architecture. The <code>pallet_eco_tracking</code> state transition function continuously audits validator energy efficiency metrics and calculates green score multipliers ($S_v$). Validators maintaining high energy efficiency receive boosted staking reward distributions from the 10B VRDX staking pool.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:16px;">
            For smart contract developers, <code>pallet-contracts</code> provides a secure WebAssembly sandbox. Contracts written in ink! are compiled into WASM binaries, ensuring deterministic gas execution, compact bytecode storage, and memory safety. The native AMM DEX pallet implements constant-product liquidity math ($x \cdot y = k$) directly inside the runtime STF, enabling instant token swaps with zero smart contract vulnerabilities.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

